  LIMITS, as registered, in both directions and not cancelling:
   · population is tracked docs/research + scripts only — a ternary in packages/ is out of
     scope, so the hazard figure is a FLOOR.
   · a common-English property name matches object literals unrelated to the member's read
     target, so the per-name site counts are an UPPER BOUND on what any one reader looks at.
   · the gap is a property of the corpus TODAY. It closes the moment anyone writes a ternary
     into one of those five property positions, and no reader changes when it does.

